fix(mcp): encode body as query string for GET/HEAD/OPTIONS

The MCP server's shared call() helper was sending a JSON body on every
request, including GET. Node fetch() rejects that with
  "fetch() request with GET/HEAD/OPTIONS method cannot have body"

This was hitting the 5 integration search tools every time the LLM
called them with a `q` argument:
  - search_serviz_belso
  - search_szev_igeny
  - search_telephely_munka
  - search_ais_motor_inventory
  - get_serviz_ticket

The /v1/integration/.../search routes are r.get() + req.query, so
encoding the body as a query string for GET methods is the right
fix and keeps the REST surface intact (no breaking change to anyone
calling those endpoints directly with ?foo=bar).

Behavior:
  - GET/HEAD/OPTIONS: body -> URLSearchParams -> query string, no body
  - POST/PUT/PATCH/DELETE: body -> JSON body, no query string
  - empty/null/undefined values are dropped from the query string
  - arrays become repeated keys (e.g. status=open&status=closed)
  - existing ?query in the path is preserved

Tests: 7 new cases in 19-mcp-call-method.test.ts cover the encoding
decision. Full suite: 301/301 pass, tsc clean.
